<title>PORTUGAL: YIELD 5.2229 ON PORTUGUESE ONE-YEAR BILLS.</title>
<headline>YIELD 5.2229 ON PORTUGUESE ONE-YEAR BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield eased to 5.2229 percent, from 5.2292 percent previously, at the Institute for Public Credit Management's sale of 364-day bills, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>The Institute placed seven billion escudos of the 20 billion on offer. The last such sale was on August 6.</p>
<p>--LISBON BUREAU 3511-3150035</p>
